  "source": {
    "post_stream": {
      "posts": [
        {
          "id": 1920666,
          "username": "Thalia_Apps",
          "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/t/da6949/{size}.png",
          "created_at": "2026-10-22T08:43:11.769Z",
          "cooked": "<p>I’ve run into a question while updating our app release checklist. Shopify’s new ‘shopify app security check’ can flag issues like ‘UNAUTHENTICATED_ENDPOINT, MISSING_TENANT_ISOLATION, COMMITTED_SECRET, and EOL_API_VERSION’.</p>\n<p>I understand the deterministic scan, but I’m less clear on the recommended workflow after it reports a finding. Should the command run in CI on every branch, or only before a release? For checks that need agent review, how are people deciding whether a finding is a real issue or a false positive?</p>\n<p>I’m also wondering how others are handling the ‘.shopify/app-security/’ output. Are you committing the findings, storing theme as CI artifacts, or keeping them local?</p>\n<p>I don’t want security checks to become something we run once before App store submission and then forget. If anyone has already added their to a real Shopify app release process, what setup has worked for you?</p>",
          "post_number": 1,
          "post_type": 1,
          "posts_count": 4,
          "updated_at": "2026-10-22T08:43:11.769Z",
          "reply_count": 0,
          "reply_to_post_number": null,
