        {
          "id": 1921041,
          "username": "umerzaman152",
          "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/community.shopify.com/umerzaman152/{size}/417113_2.png",
          "created_at": "2026-10-22T21:25:15.150Z",
          "cooked": "<p>Haven’t added this one to a real release process yet, but here’s how I’d set it up.</p>\n<p>I’d run the deterministic scan on every PR. It’s quick, so no reason to wait, and I’d fail the build on stuff like committed secrets or old API versions.</p>\n<p>The agent review I’d only run before releases, or when a PR touches auth or data access. If something’s a false positive, just note why in the PR so nobody has to look at it again next time.</p>\n<p>For the output folder, I’d keep it as a CI artifact and not commit it. Those findings can say a lot about your endpoints.</p>",
          "post_number": 3,
          "post_type": 1,
          "posts_count": 4,
          "updated_at": "2026-10-22T21:25:15.150Z",
